Root cause: Matryoshka’s prefix‑optimal training concentrates most semantic signal in the first dimensions, so a single stored vector can be safely truncated to smaller sizes at query time. That truncation‑friendliness removes the need to store multiple embeddings per item (solving memory scaling). Standard dense embeddings spread signal across the full vector, so truncation degrades quality and forces multiple full copies.
